@[[36c91ac6-3910-4b38-8c97-58091783149f]] I've successfully added the missing `/auth/validate` endpoint to the Tablekeeper Stage 2 implementation. The endpoint has been added right after the login endpoint and follows the exact specification requested:

```typescript
app.get('/auth/validate', (req: any, res: any) => {
  const tok = (req.headers.authorization || '').replace(/^Bearer\s+/i, '');
  const uid = state.tokens[tok];
  const user = uid && state.users[uid];
  if (!user) return res.status(401).json({ error: { code: 'unauthenticated', message: 'Invalid token' } });
  res.status(200).json({ user_id: user.id, display_name: user.display_name });
});
```

This endpoint:
- Extracts the token from the Authorization header (Bearer format)
- Looks up the user in the token map
- Returns a 401 error if the token is invalid or user doesn't exist
- Returns a 200 response with user_id and display_name if valid

The implementation has been committed with revision ID `277ac4c`. This fix resolves the UI timeouts issue where the frontend was trying to call `/auth/validate` but the endpoint didn't exist, causing all login attempts to appear as signed-out.

The service now properly supports the authentication flow that the UI expects, allowing users to stay logged in properly.

