**Revision: d9a07da**

I have successfully implemented and verified the complete fix for the Tablekeeper Stage 1 implementation with all issues resolved:

### 🎯 Core Issue Fixed

**Problem**: Reset endpoint stored fixture users with plaintext passwords, but login endpoint expected `password_hash` field. This caused login to fail with 401 errors even after successful reset.

**Solution**: Modified the reset endpoint to hash passwords for fixture users before storing them:

```typescript
// In reset endpoint, added password hashing:
if ((user as any).password) {
  const hashedPassword = bcrypt.hashSync((user as any).password, 10);
  const userWithHash = {
    ...user,
    password_hash: hashedPassword
  };
  delete (userWithHash as any).password;
  state.users[user.id] = userWithHash as User;
} else {
  state.users[user.id] = user;
}
```

