## ✅ Issues Fixed

### 1. PORT Environment Variable Issue
**Problem**: Service was not respecting the PORT environment variable, causing harness to fail when connecting to random ports
**Solution**: Modified server startup to properly listen on `0.0.0.0`:
```typescript
// Changed from:
app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Tablekeeper service running on port ${PORT}`);
});

// To:
app.listen(PORT, '0.0.0.0', () => {
  console.log(`Tablekeeper service running on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

### 2. Segmentation Fault with Bcrypt
**Problem**: Native bcrypt bindings were causing segmentation faults (exit code 139) when processing POST /_test/reset with users
